      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "We need to use the order of operations, also known as PEMDAS: Parentheses, Exponents, Multiplication and Division (from left to right), Addition and Subtraction (from left to right). Therefore,\n$$1+ 6\\cdot 2 - 3 + 5\\cdot4\\div2 =1 + 12 - 3 + 20\\div2 \\stackrel{\\cancel{\\text{Addition}}}{=}1 + 12 - 3 + \\cancelto{10}{\\frac{20}{2}}.$$\nSo,\n$$1+ 6\\cdot 2 - 3 + 5\\cdot4\\div2 =1 +12 - 3 + 10 =1 + 14 =\\boxed{15}.$$ Note that in the original post, the sign after the parentheses is accidentally x  two times instead of divided by two.\nAlso note that the meaning to solve this problem was that they wanted to perform things inside-in, so it matters which order which you do all the operations in.\n\nThe correct answer is 15. But if you are asked to do the operation in the singular way presented almost by the author then you get the answer different from 15 ;)\n\nSo is it a solution like $1+6\\cdot2-3+5\\div4\\cdot2$\n\nYou aren't given enough information.\n\n$1+12-3+10=10$",
